<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jagat Singh of Nurpur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1646</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jagat Singh was a Pathania Raja of Nurpur in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> hills, son of Raja Basu. He served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> as a commander, including campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, but rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> in 1641–1642. After a long siege of his forts he submitted and was pardoned, and he died in Mughal service.</p></div>
